## 1. You are one of {{ word(n_teams) }} teams

You play {{ team.nation }}: $archetype_lower. $summary

You are not on anyone's side by default. {{ others }} each want something from you, and you want something from each of them. That is your strength: a deal with one team can change the balance against another, and you can walk away from a deal that stops paying. It is also your risk: if the other teams decide you are the problem, they can work together against you.

- **Talk to everyone.** You may ask for a parley with any team, or with several at once ({% if rules == "full" %}Rules Handbook §2.6{% else %}Basic Rules §5.3{% endif %}). Agreements made there happen, with no roll.
- **Spend your Cons where they matter.** In your Cons slot you give up to three Cons in total, against any of the other teams' COAs. You don't have to answer every COA.
- **Expect to be argued about.** The other teams may make COAs aimed at you, and may agree a deal about you. Watch for it, and make your own COAs first.

